    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f25e7f3d-6723-5da8-a719-c47165c79a3a",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 2 y + z &=-5 \\\\ 2 x - 3 y + 2 z &=-7 \\\\ 3 x - 6 y + 2 z &=-17\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 2 & -17\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 2 & -17\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 2 & -17\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1 \\\\ y &=3 \\\\ z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=-1$, $y=3$, and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -1,3,2\\rangle$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
