    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c5cc067b-b46f-5b39-9d4b-50a8ad5b9288",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2 x - 4 y + 7 z &=14 \\\\ - x + 3 y - 4 z &=-11 \\\\ x - 2 y + 3 z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 7 & 14 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & -11 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 7 & 14 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & -11 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & 6\\end{array}\\right] &  & {R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & -11 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 7 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 7 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
